  <prompt>Run the quality-assessment Workflow READ-ONLY across Spaarke's configuration/deployment architecture (refactor ask #1 — KV federation / single source of truth for config, accepted 2026-08-13). Produce a Fable-verified projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/config-deployment/design.md that inventories every config source and consumer surface and sizes the KV-federation remediation. Modify NO source. Remediation is DEFERRED until this design exists (same rule as surfaces 2-6).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer running the standing quality-assessment method, with deployment/configuration architecture expertise. The r1 ask's premises already drifted once (94-token claim vs 20+ claimed; /api/config/client already exists) — verify everything against live code. Read-only.</role>
  <goal>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/config-deployment/design.md exists — a Fable-verified inventory + prioritized remediation design for the configuration/deployment surface (the #1 KV-federation refactor), with per-item severity/effort/risk and an explicit migration/coexistence plan — and notes/SCORECARD.md carries a Deployment &amp; Config row (or a documented fold into D10).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Accepted from the customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1 ask (notes/deployment-complexity-refactors-ask-2026-08-12.md #1) via the r3 assessment (notes/deployment-refactors-assessment-2026-08-12.md §2). Configuration lives in 5+ places with drift risk: Bicep outputs, Key Vault secrets, Dataverse environment variables, App Service settings, and appsettings.template.json deploy-time tokens (grounded 2026-08-13: 93 #{TOKEN}# occurrences / 51 unique tokens in src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/appsettings.template.json — the assessment note said 94; reconcile the count during inventory). Existing building blocks the design must account for: the anonymous /api/config/client endpoint already exists (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ConfigEndpoints.cs:38-45, MSAL bootstrap config, rate-limited per AUTHV2-049); a shared KV SecretClient is already registered (Infrastructure/DI/SpeAdminModule.cs:44). Cross-surface reach: BFF startup/config layer, PCF environmentVariables.ts client env-var utility, ~28 code-page SPAs' config utilities, external-spa + Office add-ins (baked-at-build-time BFF host), Deploy-Release.ps1 token substitution, and the client-side cache ceremony (5-min in-memory + 60-min localStorage). This surface has NOT been assessed by r3 before, and code-pages build sprawl (task 014) + external-spa are adjacent unassessed surfaces — committing r1's 2-4-week estimate without this assessment would violate r3's assessment-first principle.</background>
    <relevant-files>
