    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Rubric D1-D11.</dependency>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">The quality-assessment workflow.</dependency>
      <dependency task="061" status="pending">SOFT (not blocking): the config-validation hardening (#2) is a stated prerequisite preference for KV-federation remediation ("validate KV-sourced config before dropping tokens") — the design must sequence remediation after 061, but this assessment can run before/alongside it.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: READ-ONLY (NFR-03) — no src/, scripts/, or .github/ modification; only outputs are the workstream design.md + SCORECARD row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: the Fable adversarial-verification pass is non-negotiable (NFR-05) — every config-source and token-count claim carries file:line evidence and survives verification.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (inventory closed set): the design MUST inventory (1) the 5 config sources (Bicep outputs, KV secrets, Dataverse env-vars, App Service settings incl. #{TOKEN}# substitution, appsettings.template.json), (2) the deploy-time token census (reconcile 93-occurrence/51-unique vs the 94 claim), (3) the existing /api/config/client endpoint + its contract, (4) the client-side cache ceremony (5-min/60-min), (5) KV-provider wiring already present (SecretClient, KV references in App Settings), and (6) the cross-surface consumer reach: BFF + PCF environmentVariables.ts + ~28 code-page SPAs + external-spa + Office add-ins + Deploy-Release.ps1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: remediation is DEFERRED — this task produces the design only; remediation tasks are created from the verified design (assessment-first, same as surfaces 2-6). The design MUST size remediation tranches and state the migration/coexistence plan (additive KV reader, per-customer cutover, token-pattern removal last).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: coordinate framing with task 014 (code-pages build sprawl assessment) — the ~28-SPA config-utility inventory overlaps; cross-reference rather than duplicate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="naming-productization-2026-08-13">Scope ADDITION (owner directive — productization): the assessment MUST include a **resource + KV-secret naming-conformance audit** against `docs/architecture/AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md` (which already mandates env-agnostic KV names at :329). Flag every violation that breaks clean multi-environment replication: (1) **env token baked into a NAME meant to be env-agnostic** (e.g. `SPRK-DEV-DATAVERSE-URL` vs the correct `DATAVERSE-URL`); (2) **casing drift** (`BFF-API-ClientSecret` vs `bff-api-client-secret`); (3) **prefix drift** (`MANAGED-IDENTITY-CLIENT-ID` vs `SPRK-MANAGED-IDENTITY-CLIENT-ID` vs `UAMI-ClientId`); (4) **orphans/duplicates** (`Graph-API-ClientSecret` with 0 consumers). Seed evidence: the dev-vault `spaarke-spekvcert` census in `notes/bff-auth-surface-map.md` §"Portal verification 2026-08-13". Output a target-name map (current → canonical, env-agnostic) that task 063 turns into the standard + gate, and that r1 uses to apply/remediate. Read-only — do NOT rename anything.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Configuration/deployment architecture assessment</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/standards/CODE-QUALITY-RUBRIC.md</file>
