    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor-level declaration (STANDARD + reason). Confirm "use a workflow" opt-in; load rubric + workflow + the two 2026-08-12 notes.</step>
    <step order="1">Fan-out: read-only finders across the six inventory areas (config sources, token census, /api/config/client, cache ceremony, KV wiring, cross-surface consumers), file:line evidence for every claim.</step>
    <step order="2">Mandatory Fable adversarial-verification stage: re-verify the token census, confirm each claimed config source actually feeds runtime behavior, and refute any "unused config source" or "dead token" claims against src/ AND tests/ AND deploy scripts.</step>
    <step order="3">If verification refutes &gt;30% of findings or cannot confirm the config-source inventory, invoke the escalation trigger.</step>
    <step order="4">Synthesize projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/config-deployment/design.md: verified inventory, drift-risk map (the one-URL-five-places class), prioritized remediation tranches with effort/risk, migration/coexistence plan, and explicit sequencing note that config-validation hardening (task 061) lands before token-pattern removal.</step>
    <step order="5">Append the Deployment &amp; Config row to notes/SCORECARD.md (or document folding into D10 per the r3 assessment §3).</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 017 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Fable verification pass cannot confirm the config-source inventory (which sources actually feed runtime config, with file:line evidence), or refutes &gt;30% of first-pass findings, STOP and report per CLAUDE.md §6 — do NOT synthesize a remediation design from unverified findings (NFR-05). A KV-federation design built on a wrong inventory would mis-scope a cross-surface refactor touching every customer deployment.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No config-deployment assessment exists: projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/ has bff-api only (Glob workstreams/*/design.md → bff-api/design.md); r1's ask (notes/deployment-complexity-refactors-ask-2026-08-12.md #1) is an unverified estimate whose premises already drifted (claimed 20+ tokens, live count 93 occurrences/51 unique; claimed /api/config/client needs building, it exists at Api/ConfigEndpoints.cs:38-45).</existing>
    <extension>No — no existing r3 task covers config architecture (task 014 covers code-pages build sprawl only; the overlap is cross-referenced, not duplicated). This is the standard per-surface assessment artifact, extending the established workstream pattern rather than a new mechanism.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without a verified design, r3 either commits a 2-4-week cross-surface refactor on drifted premises (mis-scoped, touching BFF + PCF + ~28 SPAs + external-spa + deploy scripts) or leaves the one-URL-five-places drift class (sprk_BffApiBaseUrl must match App Service URL, redirect URIs, CORS AllowedOrigins, PowerPages BaseUrl) unmanaged per-customer — the exact silent-fail class (T1/T5) r1 catalogued.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/config-deployment/design.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/SCORECARD.md (Deployment &amp; Config row appended, or documented D10 fold)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/workstreams/config-deployment/design.md exists, Fable-verified, covering all six inventory areas with file:line evidence and a reconciled token census.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the design, remediation is sized in tranches with a migration/coexistence plan, and NO remediation was executed by this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the design, the sequencing dependency on task 061 (fail-fast validation before token-pattern removal) is explicit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, notes/SCORECARD.md carries the surface's row (or a documented fold into D10).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no file under src/, scripts/, or .github/ was modified (read-only assessment).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: if Fable verification could not confirm the inventory, no design.md was synthesized (escalation fired instead).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Refactor ask #1 (KV federation) — accepted 2026-08-13 into r3 as assess-first (project CLAUDE.md decision 2026-08-13). Read-only ⇒ conflict-free ⇒ can run anytime P1 capacity allows. Remediation tasks created only after this design exists. Adjacent: task 014 (code-pages), task 061 (#2 fail-fast validation — soft prerequisite for remediation, not for this assessment).</notes>

